WEBVTT

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.980
Ok, I explain the big rules of chess,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.240
like that you will look perfectly comfortable when

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.800
people will talk about it around you.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.420
This is a video for beginners, so pros

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.280
you can swipe.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.000
In fact, a game of chess is played

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.900
between two players and each has 16 pieces.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.520
So you told me, it's 32 pieces on

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.340
a 64-box board.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.320
Because yes, it is on this board that

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.320
we call a chessboard that the game will

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:22.740
unfold.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.500
The chessboard is composed of 8 lines numbered

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.800
from 1 to 8 and 8 columns from

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.620
A to H.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.240
Each player starts with exactly the same number

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:31.780
of pieces.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.040
8 pawns, 2 rooks, 2 knights, 2 pawns,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.480
a queen and a king.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.960
And the goal of the game is simple,

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.020
put the opponent's king in checkmate.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.760
It is also said that he is checkmate

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.840
when he is attacked and that he can

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.640
not be defended or escape.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.420
You should know absolutely that each piece has

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.640
its own way of moving.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.060
The pawns, they move straight ahead of a

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.300
single box, but they can eat the other

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.060
pieces diagonally, like that.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.420
The rooks move in a straight line, so

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.300
like that or like that, of the number

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.220
of boxes they want.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.820
And it's the same thing for the pawns,

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.379
but they are diagonally.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.980
The knights, they make movements in wings, like

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:07.180
that.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.600
And it's the only ones who can jump

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.920
over the other pieces.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.240
The queen, she is the strongest piece.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.520
She can go anywhere, in a line or

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.680
diagonally, of the number of boxes she wants.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.640
And the king, he only moves from one

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.280
box at a time.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.060
So as much to say that some pieces

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.760
are much more powerful than others.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.360
What you also need to know is that

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.280
the game always starts with the blocks.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.880
For during this game, there are also special

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:28.980
rules.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.520
For example, there is the rook.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.540
The rook, it allows you to protect your

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.260
king and move a tower at the same

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.460
time.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.520
The promotion is when a pawn arrives at

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:37.140
the end of the board.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.800
And when he does, he can turn into

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.540
a queen or any other chosen piece.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.100
That's why you have to keep your pawns

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.160
on the chessboard as much as possible and

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.580
make them move intelligently.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.680
At each turn, each player plays a move.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.820
And the goal is to build a strategy

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.740
to trap your opponent, protect your king and

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.740
attack at the right time.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.340
And at the end, when the king can

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.160
no longer move without being captured, it's chess

00:01:59.160 --> 00:01:59.660
and maths.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.120
And the game is over.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.760
Now you know the basic rules of chess,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.080
although there are still subtleties.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.860
And do not forget to subscribe to know

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.220
the rules of other sports.

